1796
01:02:17,300 --> 01:02:20,020
-Packed with minerals,
 Booze really satisfies.

1797
01:02:20,020 --> 01:02:21,790
-Ooh, could I lick the glass?

1798
01:02:21,790 --> 01:02:22,460
-Oh, Wendy.

1799
01:02:29,380 --> 01:02:31,250
-A directory for the alley.

1800
01:02:31,250 --> 01:02:32,910
-Well, each bum has
 a listing, there.

1801
01:02:32,910 --> 01:02:34,450
-Look at all the neat shops.

1802
01:02:39,830 --> 01:02:42,080
(IMITATING SEDUCTIVE FEMALE
 VOICE) Going up, Mr. Chaney?

1803
01:02:42,080 --> 01:02:44,960
-Uh, next up, the food court--
 Taco John's, One Potato, Two,

1804
01:02:44,960 --> 01:02:48,380
Great American Hotdog
 Experience, Puffy's.

1805
01:02:48,380 --> 01:02:48,880
-Puffy's?

1806
01:02:51,780 --> 01:02:55,270
-Well, I may be indestructible,
 but I'm ruled by my tummy.

1807
01:02:55,270 --> 01:02:57,340
[CHUCKLES] It says lunchtime.

1808
01:02:57,340 --> 01:02:59,820
-Hey, could you imagine
 a big indestructible snag

1809
01:02:59,820 --> 01:03:00,400
off this thing?

1810
01:03:00,400 --> 01:03:00,900
-Oh, yuck.

1811
01:03:00,900 --> 01:03:01,570
-It'd kill somebody.

1812
01:03:01,570 --> 01:03:02,340
-Snicker-snag Triple.

1813
01:03:06,230 --> 01:03:06,730
-Hey!

1814
01:03:06,730 --> 01:03:08,690
That's ocupado, pal!

1815
01:03:11,890 --> 01:03:15,480
-Hey, look he's in
 the cleaver den.

1816
01:03:15,480 --> 01:03:16,320
-Oh.

1817
01:03:16,320 --> 01:03:17,180
-Excuse me.

1818
01:03:17,180 --> 01:03:19,090
Just adding a few
 loose ends, here.

1819
01:03:21,970 --> 01:03:24,300
-Look, he's casting
 Richard Nixon's shadow.

1820
01:03:24,300 --> 01:03:25,290
-Oh, my goodness.

1821
01:03:28,130 --> 01:03:30,460
-[GUFFAWS] (STUPIDLY) Just
 gonna steal a few Post-it notes.

1822
01:03:30,460 --> 01:03:31,890
Yep.

1823
01:03:31,890 --> 01:03:34,000
-(MUFFLED) If you'd
 like to make a call--

1824
01:03:34,000 --> 01:03:37,240
-He's really very thorough.

1825
01:03:37,240 --> 01:03:44,430
-Now I'm going to rearrange his
 filing system. [LAUGHS EVILLY]

1826
01:03:44,430 --> 01:03:47,210
-Looks like he's wearing a
 catcher's mitt around his neck.

1827
01:03:50,610 --> 01:03:53,530
-Say.

1828
01:03:53,530 --> 01:03:56,200
-We'll be back after
 these messages.

1829
01:03:56,200 --> 01:03:56,770
-Needs a shave.

1830
01:03:59,440 --> 01:04:02,130
-(NEW JERSEY ACCENT)
 Jeez, my appendix burst.

1831
01:04:02,130 --> 01:04:02,840
-It's Tom Landy.

1832
01:04:08,480 --> 01:04:09,890
-Squeamy, is that you?

1833
01:04:14,160 --> 01:04:17,420
-[LAUGHS_STUPIDLY] I have a
 sweet tooth-- for revenge.

1834
01:04:20,830 --> 01:04:23,740
-Kind of an enigmatic smile.

1835
01:04:23,740 --> 01:04:24,440
-Hello?

1836
01:04:24,440 --> 01:04:25,150
-Watch me rock.

1837
01:04:32,380 --> 01:04:36,020
-Smooth operator-- huh!

1838
01:04:36,020 --> 01:04:38,990
-I mind very much if you smoke.

1839
01:04:38,990 --> 01:04:40,930
[GUNFIRE]

1840
01:04:40,930 --> 01:04:43,800
-Missed me, missed me,
 now you gotta kiss me.

1841
01:04:43,800 --> 01:04:46,480
-Hey, didn't you see the
 first part of this movie?

1842
01:04:51,270 --> 01:04:52,710
-Got him.

1843
01:04:52,710 --> 01:04:53,670
-[SCREAMS]

1844
01:04:53,670 --> 01:04:56,160
-Scream all you want,
 but take all you scream.

1845
01:04:56,160 --> 01:04:57,010
-[CONTINUES_SCREAMING]

1846
01:04:57,010 --> 01:04:59,010
-Linda Lavin?

1847
01:04:59,010 --> 01:05:02,000
-[WOMAN_SCREAMS]

1848
01:05:02,000 --> 01:05:03,500
-Plop.

1849
01:05:03,500 --> 01:05:07,850
-Yep, he didn't come
 out of his tuck in time.

1850
01:05:07,850 --> 01:05:09,440
-Ah, that's nice.

1851
01:05:09,440 --> 01:05:11,440
I'm tired now, but it's
 a good kind of tired.

1852
01:05:11,440 --> 01:05:14,310
Ah.

1853
01:05:14,310 --> 01:05:16,660
-Sara, get me my pilot.

1854
01:05:16,660 --> 01:05:17,340
-Operator?

1855
01:05:17,340 --> 01:05:19,200
Get me the police!

1856
01:05:19,200 --> 01:05:20,870
(FRANTICALLY) Police!

1857
01:05:20,870 --> 01:05:21,370
Yes!

1858
01:05:21,370 --> 01:05:24,000
-Did she say please or police?

1859
01:05:24,000 --> 01:05:26,230
-C'mon, boxcars,
 baby needs a new pair

1860
01:05:26,230 --> 01:05:27,320
of indestructible shoes.

1861
01:05:30,490 --> 01:05:33,760
-What are they waiting
 for, a putty knife?

1862
01:05:33,760 --> 01:05:34,670
-It kinda looks like rice.

1863
01:05:37,290 --> 01:05:38,710
-What's happened?

1864
01:05:38,710 --> 01:05:41,310
-Guy named Squeamy got
 thrown from the fifth floor.

1865
01:05:41,310 --> 01:05:42,570
-Now they call him Squishy.

1866
01:05:42,570 --> 01:05:43,640
-Customer of mine.

1867
01:05:43,640 --> 01:05:44,140
-Tuh!

1868
01:05:44,140 --> 01:05:45,050
-You mean Squeamy Ellis?

1869
01:05:45,050 --> 01:05:45,910
-Yeah, that's him.

1870
01:05:45,910 --> 01:05:46,980
-How many Squeamies do you know?

1871
01:05:46,980 --> 01:05:47,540
-Just Squeamy?

1872
01:05:47,540 --> 01:05:48,940
No-- No one else was killed.

1873
01:05:48,940 --> 01:05:50,930
-Ain't one enough?

1874
01:05:50,930 --> 01:05:53,470
-Wow, everybody's so touchy
 at the scene of a death.

1875
01:05:56,880 --> 01:06:00,610
-Hulk, you pull the
 car over right now.

1876
01:06:00,610 --> 01:06:02,820
-I tell you, the bullets
 never even phased him.

1877
01:06:02,820 --> 01:06:04,360
-Ah, the whole cast is there.

1878
01:06:04,360 --> 01:06:06,300
-Wow.

1879
01:06:06,300 --> 01:06:07,980
-God help us if the
 papers get a hold of this.

1880
01:06:07,980 --> 01:06:09,710
-(IRISH ACCENT) All right,
 gather around, everybody.

1881
01:06:09,710 --> 01:06:10,480
Lots to see.

1882
01:06:10,480 --> 01:06:11,970
Show's just starting.

1883
01:06:11,970 --> 01:06:13,380
-We're gonna stake out
 on Joe Marcellia's.

1884
01:06:13,380 --> 01:06:14,380
-John Huston.

1885
01:06:14,380 --> 01:06:15,330
-No.

1886
01:06:15,330 --> 01:06:17,140
-Lauder, I'm going
 to call San Quentin.

1887
01:06:17,140 --> 01:06:18,880
Suppose Benton is alive.

1888
01:06:18,880 --> 01:06:21,340
-Every available man's
 been put on the case now.

1889
01:06:21,340 --> 01:06:21,840
Yes, sir.

1890
01:06:21,840 --> 01:06:23,230
All right.

1891
01:06:23,230 --> 01:06:24,700
All right!

1892
01:06:24,700 --> 01:06:25,330
Anything new?

1893
01:06:25,330 --> 01:06:27,200
-Well, remember when I got
 ahead of myself a while back?

1894
01:06:27,200 --> 01:06:28,350
Well, we're at that scene now.

1895
01:06:28,350 --> 01:06:30,450
-San Francisco police
 located his laboratory

1896
01:06:30,450 --> 01:06:32,690
in the basement of an electrical
 power receiving station.

1897
01:06:32,690 --> 01:06:33,970
-Bradshaw, what's he know?

1898
01:06:33,970 --> 01:06:34,950
-He's dead.

1899
01:06:34,950 --> 01:06:36,900
And another man
 too, his assistant.

1900
01:06:36,900 --> 01:06:38,300
The lab is a shambles.

1901
01:06:38,300 --> 01:06:39,270
-So's my heart.

1902
01:06:39,270 --> 01:06:41,770
-Now we're getting some
 action from San Francisco.

1903
01:06:41,770 --> 01:06:44,090
Benton's body never
 arrived at the mortuary

1904
01:06:44,090 --> 01:06:45,530
where it was supposed to go.

1905
01:06:45,530 --> 01:06:47,850
An attendant there
 finally broke down--

1906
01:06:47,850 --> 01:06:49,220
-That's not a very good poem.

1907
01:06:49,220 --> 01:06:49,820
Meter's all wrong.

1908
01:06:49,820 --> 01:06:52,870
-By handing the body over to a
 man he was unable to identify.

1909
01:06:52,870 --> 01:06:55,070
The man was driving
 a station wagon.

1910
01:06:55,070 --> 01:06:57,910
-Oh my god, that's a symbol
 of American suburban life!

1911
01:06:57,910 --> 01:06:59,980
-The commissioner's are on his,
 and the mayor's are on theirs.

1912
01:06:59,980 --> 01:07:03,050
Now am I supposed to tell them
 that our killer is a dead man?

1913
01:07:03,050 --> 01:07:05,810
-They found a notebook
 in Bradshaw's lab.

1914
01:07:05,810 --> 01:07:07,100
-It said, [SCREAM].

1915
01:07:07,100 --> 01:07:09,380
-With a professor
 Dwiggins at Caltech.

1916
01:07:09,380 --> 01:07:11,300
I hope to hear
 from Dwiggins soon.

1917
01:07:11,300 --> 01:07:13,380
-Captain, report
 from the Valley,

1918
01:07:13,380 --> 01:07:14,340
on the hysterical woman.

1919
01:07:14,340 --> 01:07:15,510
Reports the presence
 of the killer.

1920
01:07:15,510 --> 01:07:16,810
-Oh, that was me.

1921
01:07:16,810 --> 01:07:18,130
Excuse me.

1922
01:07:18,130 --> 01:07:20,200
-Let's go.

1923
01:07:20,200 --> 01:07:21,700
-(SINGING) There's a
 monster in the valley,

1924
01:07:21,700 --> 01:07:23,200
and he's prowling in the alley!

1925
01:07:23,200 --> 01:07:24,480
-Hey, check this out, Vern.

1926
01:07:24,480 --> 01:07:26,850
When I let go of the steering
 wheel, it pulls to the left.

1927
01:07:26,850 --> 01:07:29,640
Isn't that something?

1928
01:07:29,640 --> 01:07:32,250
-We were just
 looking for agates.

1929
01:07:32,250 --> 01:07:35,320
-It's Ma Barker's killer brood.

1930
01:07:35,320 --> 01:07:36,850
-OK, blow hard.

1931
01:07:36,850 --> 01:07:37,980
There you go.

1932
01:07:37,980 --> 01:07:39,820
-Now, you and your boyfriend
 had a little fight,

1933
01:07:39,820 --> 01:07:41,830
and he got out of the
 car to take a walk.

1934
01:07:41,830 --> 01:07:42,660
-Uh-huh.

1935
01:07:42,660 --> 01:07:44,600
-You noticed that he
 walked down towards the sun

1936
01:07:44,600 --> 01:07:46,480
fair in the direction where
 you've seen those lights.

1937
01:07:46,480 --> 01:07:47,060
-Uh-huh.

1938
01:07:47,060 --> 01:07:47,560
-Before.

1939
01:07:47,560 --> 01:07:48,200
-Uh-huh.

1940
01:07:48,200 --> 01:07:49,840
-What happened then, Miss?

1941
01:07:49,840 --> 01:07:51,060
Please try to tell us.

1942
01:07:51,060 --> 01:07:52,530
-Go! [MAKES TICKING SOUND]

1943
01:07:52,530 --> 01:07:57,160
-Well, I just sat there,
 a few minutes, I guess.

1944
01:07:57,160 --> 01:07:58,040
I was pretty mad.

1945
01:07:58,040 --> 01:07:59,870
-(IMITATING FEMALE VOICE) I
 was fluffing in my car, OK?

1946
01:07:59,870 --> 01:08:03,880
-There was a loud
 crash, like heavy metal.

1947
01:08:03,880 --> 01:08:04,610
-She's only a bust.

1948
01:08:04,610 --> 01:08:06,400
-From down here.

1949
01:08:06,400 --> 01:08:09,990
I got out of the car
 to get a better look.

1950
01:08:09,990 --> 01:08:13,120
I heard Jimmy cry out something.

1951
01:08:13,120 --> 01:08:15,330
-You said Jimmy Smits?

1952
01:08:15,330 --> 01:08:16,730
-Then, down here--

1953
01:08:16,730 --> 01:08:17,740
-I wish you'd blink.

1954
01:08:17,740 --> 01:08:19,040
-A patch of lights.

1955
01:08:19,040 --> 01:08:19,610
-It's like blank.

1956
01:08:19,610 --> 01:08:20,720
-That's incredible.

1957
01:08:20,720 --> 01:08:21,770
-Really spooky.

1958
01:08:21,770 --> 01:08:22,710
-Blink, hello!

1959
01:08:22,710 --> 01:08:23,310
Blink!

1960
01:08:23,310 --> 01:08:23,930
-Blink!

1961
01:08:23,930 --> 01:08:24,990
-Bliiink!

1962
01:08:24,990 --> 01:08:26,790
-Like a zombie, blink!

1963
01:08:26,790 --> 01:08:29,670
-A big man lifted Jimmy up--

1964
01:08:29,670 --> 01:08:30,170
-Please!

1965
01:08:30,170 --> 01:08:31,290
-Over his head like--

1966
01:08:31,290 --> 01:08:32,870
-She's stuck in
 Marsha Mason mode!

1967
01:08:32,870 --> 01:08:34,770
-Like he didn't weigh a thing.

1968
01:08:34,770 --> 01:08:36,370
-Jimmy screamed.

1969
01:08:36,370 --> 01:08:37,880
Just once.

1970
01:08:37,880 --> 01:08:38,540
-Go!

1971
01:08:38,540 --> 01:08:39,810
-Blink.

1972
01:08:39,810 --> 01:08:41,340
-Please, blink!

1973
01:08:41,340 --> 01:08:42,290
-What's she looking at?

1974
01:08:42,290 --> 01:08:43,230
-I heard it snap!

1975
01:08:43,230 --> 01:08:46,180
-It sounded like celery!

1976
01:08:46,180 --> 01:08:50,070
-Then I-- I started running
 till I found the tide.

1977
01:08:50,070 --> 01:08:52,840
They let me use
 the phone. [SOBS]

1978
01:08:52,840 --> 01:08:56,780
-But--I didn't have friends
 and family! [MOCK_CRIES]

1979
01:08:56,780 --> 01:08:57,670
-Thank you, Miss.

1980
01:08:57,670 --> 01:08:58,340
-[CONTINUES_SOBBING]

1981
01:08:58,340 --> 01:08:59,160
-Can I have my tie back?

1982
01:09:03,110 --> 01:09:05,660
-O'Malley, see that the young
 lady gets home all right.

1983
01:09:05,660 --> 01:09:06,990
-Does it have to be her home?

1984
01:09:06,990 --> 01:09:09,310
I'm kidding, of course.

1985
01:09:09,310 --> 01:09:12,050
-Paul Lowe, while
 driving to his office,

1986
01:09:12,050 --> 01:09:15,130
heard a radio commentator report
 the murder of Joe Marcellia.

1987
01:09:15,130 --> 01:09:16,030
And what shocked him most--

1988
01:09:16,030 --> 01:09:17,480
-(SINGING) I want to
 know what love is.

1989
01:09:17,480 --> 01:09:18,980
-Was when the broadcast
 identified the killer

1990
01:09:18,980 --> 01:09:21,550
as possibly being the Butcher.

1991
01:09:21,550 --> 01:09:23,750
Lowe headed straight for
 Eva Martin at the burlesque.

1992
01:09:23,750 --> 01:09:24,580
-But who doesn't?

1993
01:09:24,580 --> 01:09:25,930
-Oh-ho-ho.

1994
01:09:25,930 --> 01:09:26,830
-Oh!

1995
01:09:26,830 --> 01:09:28,470
You gave me a start, Mr. Lowe.

1996
01:09:28,470 --> 01:09:29,830
-Is this where a corsage goes?

1997
01:09:29,830 --> 01:09:30,760
-Well, I'm taking her place.

1998
01:09:30,760 --> 01:09:33,060
I'm gonna wear her costume.

1999
01:09:33,060 --> 01:09:34,050
What's it to you?

2000
01:09:34,050 --> 01:09:35,670
-I asked you, where's Eva?

2001
01:09:35,670 --> 01:09:37,070
-Hey, don't get physical.

2002
01:09:37,070 --> 01:09:38,190
-Let me hear your body talk.

2003
01:09:38,190 --> 01:09:39,750
-Then watch the tone
 of voice, buster.

2004
01:09:39,750 --> 01:09:41,990
I told you, little
 Eva isn't here.

2005
01:09:41,990 --> 01:09:43,110
-I can see that for myself.

2006
01:09:43,110 --> 01:09:44,270
Where is she?

2007
01:09:44,270 --> 01:09:45,170
-[GIGGLES]

2008
01:09:45,170 --> 01:09:46,900
-Hmm, looks like she's
 wearing Fruit of the Loins.

2009
01:09:46,900 --> 01:09:47,400
-Oh.

2010
01:09:47,400 --> 01:09:47,900
-Oohh.

2011
01:09:47,900 --> 01:09:49,600
-That's where she is.

2012
01:09:49,600 --> 01:09:52,050
-Yes, sir.

2013
01:09:52,050 --> 01:09:53,930
-No sir, Captain Lauder's
 still with the mayor.

2014
01:09:53,930 --> 01:09:55,260
-No, I'll get out of
 your officer, sir.

2015
01:09:55,260 --> 01:09:57,910
As soon as poss-- yes,
 I'm putting the cigarette

2016
01:09:57,910 --> 01:09:59,230
out now, sir.

2017
01:09:59,230 --> 01:09:59,990
Yeah.

2018
01:09:59,990 --> 01:10:02,270
-Yes sir, we-- we
 know he's dangerous.

2019
01:10:02,270 --> 01:10:02,830
Every angle.

2020
01:10:02,830 --> 01:10:05,300
-He's the other end of
 a Bob Newhart routine.

2021
01:10:05,300 --> 01:10:08,270
-Yes sir, I-- I'll tell him.

2022
01:10:08,270 --> 01:10:11,260
-We'll have to swing by the
 7-Eleven and pick him up.

2023
01:10:14,960 --> 01:10:16,020
-Well, Mr. Wiggins.

2024
01:10:21,180 --> 01:10:22,140
-Huh.

2025
01:10:22,140 --> 01:10:23,330
-What the heel are you doing?

2026
01:10:27,060 --> 01:10:29,610
-Here, ma'am, I'll just
 wear my cop shoes home.

2027
01:10:29,610 --> 01:10:31,120
-Thanks.

2028
01:10:31,120 --> 01:10:32,220
-(IMITATES FEMALE
 VOICE) How come

2029
01:10:32,220 --> 01:10:33,300
there's powdered sugar in them?

2030
01:10:33,300 --> 01:10:35,070
-Hey, cut with the
 doughnut remarks.

2031
01:10:35,070 --> 01:10:36,980
-Ah, jokes.

2032
01:10:36,980 --> 01:10:45,520
[DOORS CLOSING]

2033
01:10:45,520 --> 01:10:46,920
-OK, Cambot, bring it in.

2034
01:10:46,920 --> 01:10:49,200
I wanna try that Lon
 Cheney eye thing.

2035
01:10:49,200 --> 01:10:50,670
Bring it in closer.

2036
01:10:50,670 --> 01:10:51,380
More.

2037
01:10:51,380 --> 01:10:51,880
More.

2038
01:10:51,880 --> 01:10:52,400
Closer.

2039
01:10:52,400 --> 01:10:53,150
Come on.

2040
01:10:53,150 --> 01:10:54,240
Come on, closer.

2041
01:10:54,240 --> 01:10:54,910
Yeah, that's good.

2042
01:10:54,910 --> 01:10:57,350
OK.

2043
01:10:57,350 --> 01:10:59,900
-(SINGING OFFSCREEN) If I can't
 have you, I don't want nobody--

2044
01:10:59,900 --> 01:11:00,490
whoa!

2045
01:11:00,490 --> 01:11:01,660
-Joel, what are you doing?

2046
01:11:01,660 --> 01:11:03,120
-I'm doing an experiment.

2047
01:11:03,120 --> 01:11:05,100
-Oh, I thought somebody had
 replaced the monitor with

2048
01:11:05,100 --> 01:11:05,840
a Jack-o'-lantern.

2049
01:11:05,840 --> 01:11:06,510
[LAUGHTER]

2050
01:11:06,510 --> 01:11:07,760
-No.

2051
01:11:07,760 --> 01:11:08,430
-Oh, bite me.

2052
01:11:08,430 --> 01:11:09,580
It's for-- ow!

2053
01:11:09,580 --> 01:11:10,690
